---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  description="How Tearleads collects, uses, protects, and deletes customer information."
  eyebrow="Privacy / 01"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="August 23, 2026"
>
  <section class="legalPromise" aria-label="Our privacy promise">
    <p class="kicker"><span></span> Our promise</p>
    <h2>We never sell customer information.</h2>
    <p>
      We do not rent customer information, give it to data brokers or
      advertisers, or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Tearleads, LLC (“Tearleads,” “we,” “us,”
      or “our”) handles information when you use our websites, applications,
      and related services (the “Service”). It applies to account holders and
      to people whose information an authorized user places in a Tearleads
      workspace.
    </p>
    <p>
      A Tearleads organization is a shared workspace. Information placed in an
      organization may be available to other authorized members of that
      organization according to their roles and group access.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account and security information</h3>
    <p>
      We collect information used to create and secure your account, such as
      your name, email address, authentication credentials in protected form,
      email-verification status, multi-factor authentication settings, active
      sessions, organization memberships, roles, and invitations.
    </p>

    <h3>Workspace information</h3>
    <p>
      We collect the information you or other authorized users add to the
      Service. Depending on the features you use, this may include business
      names, EINs, incorporation dates, addresses, documents, uploaded files,
      inbound emails and attachments, audit templates and results, issue
      assignments, notes, labels, and related activity records.
    </p>

    <h3>Financial information from Plaid</h3>
    <p>
      If you choose to connect a financial institution, we use Plaid to request
      up to 24 months of account and transaction history. We may receive and
      store:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        institution and account details, including institution name, account
        name, account type and subtype, account mask, balances, and currency;
      </li>
      <li>
        transaction details, including transaction and authorization dates,
        amount, currency, merchant or description, category, payment channel,
        and pending status; and
      </li>
      <li>
        Plaid-generated identifiers, synchronization state, and an encrypted
        access token needed to refresh the connection.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not receive or store the username and password you enter into Plaid
      Link for your financial institution. Plaid and your financial institution
      handle that connection.
    </p>

    <h3>Technical information</h3>
    <p>
      We and our infrastructure providers may process IP address, browser and
      device information, request timestamps, security events, and diagnostic
      logs. The Service also uses cookies and browser storage that are necessary
      for authentication, account switching, preferences, and Plaid connection
      flows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>provide, operate, synchronize, and maintain the Service;</li>
      <li>
        display and help authorized users organize files, messages, audits,
        businesses, accounts, and transactions;
      </li>
      <li>
        authenticate users, enforce organization permissions, prevent fraud and
        abuse, and protect the Service;
      </li>
      <li>respond to requests, troubleshoot problems, and improve reliability;</li>
      <li>comply with law and enforce our agreements.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not use customer financial data to advertise to you or to make
      lending, credit, insurance, or employment decisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Plaid and connected financial accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Plaid processes information when you use Plaid Link and when it maintains
      a connection to your financial institution. Plaid’s handling of that
      information is governed by the
      {" "}<a href="https://plaid.com/legal/#consumers">Plaid End User Privacy Policy</a>.
      You should review it before connecting an account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tearleads uses Plaid data to import, synchronize, display, filter,
      reconcile, and let authorized organization members annotate financial
      accounts and transactions. We request only the Plaid Transactions data
      used for these features. You may disconnect an institution in the Finance
      page or manage your Plaid connections through
      {" "}<a href="https://my.plaid.com/">Plaid Portal</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. How we disclose information</h2>
    <p>We may disclose information only as needed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Within your organization.</strong> Authorized workspace members
        can access organization information based on their roles and groups.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To service providers.</strong> Providers such as Cloudflare and
        Plaid process information for hosting, storage, security, email, and
        financial connectivity under their agreements with us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>For legal and safety reasons.</strong> We may disclose information
        if reasonably necessary to comply with law, lawful process, or to protect
        people, rights, and the security of the Service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>In a business transaction.</strong> Information may transfer as
        part of a merger, financing, acquisition, reorganization, or sale of
        assets, subject to this Policy and applicable law.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>At your direction.</strong> We may disclose information when you
        or an authorized organization administrator directs us to do so.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These disclosures are not sales of customer information. We will never
      sell customer information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use administrative and technical safeguards designed to protect
      customer information. These include encrypted network connections,
      organization-scoped access controls, optional multi-factor authentication,
      monitoring, and encryption of Plaid access tokens before storage. No
      method of storage or transmission is completely secure, so we cannot
      guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      We retain information while it is needed to provide the Service, meet
      legal obligations, resolve disputes, and protect the Service. Retention
      also depends on the controls available for each feature:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Disconnecting a financial institution revokes Plaid access and removes
        the stored access token, but retains previously imported accounts,
        transactions, and annotations so you do not lose your records.
      </li>
      <li>
        After disconnecting, an authorized user can permanently delete that
        institution’s imported financial data from the Finance page.
      </li>
      <li>
        Deleted inbound emails remain in Trash and become eligible for
        permanent deletion after 30 days, unless restored sooner.
      </li>
      <li>
        A deleted organization becomes inaccessible immediately and is
        eligible for permanent deletion with its organization data after 30
        days, unless an administrator restores it sooner.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Limited records may remain longer when required by law, necessary for
      security or fraud prevention, or present in disaster-recovery backups
      until those backups expire.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access,
      correction, deletion, portability, or restriction of certain personal
      information. You may also have the right to appeal a response or complain
      to a privacy regulator. We may need to verify your identity and authority
      before acting on a request.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the Service’s organization, inbox, and Finance controls where
      available. For other privacy requests, email
      {" "}<a href="mailto:privacy@tearleads.com">privacy@tearleads.com</a>. Plaid
      also provides independent connection and data controls through Plaid
      Portal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed to children under 18, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children under 18.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Changes to this Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Policy as the Service or law changes. We will post the
      updated version here and change its effective date. If a change materially
      affects how we use previously collected information, we will provide
      additional notice when required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests about this Policy can be sent to
      {" "}<a href="mailto:privacy@tearleads.com">privacy@tearleads.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
